    "description": "<p>A Utility Belt has 10 pouches containing a standard array of items. Each pouch can carry 0.5 kg. </p><p>The standard Utility Belt has the following items: </p><table class=\"wikitable\"> \n <tbody>\n  <tr> \n   <th>ITEM </th> \n   <th>COST </th> \n   <th>WEIGHT </th>\n  </tr> \n  <tr> \n   <td><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Ration_Pack\" title=\"Ration Pack\">Ration Pack</a> (x3) </td> \n   <td>15 </td> \n   <td>0.3 kg </td>\n  </tr> \n  <tr> \n   <td><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Medpac\" title=\"Medpac\">Medpac</a> </td> \n   <td>100 </td> \n   <td>1 kg </td>\n  </tr> \n  <tr> \n   <td><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Tool_Kit\" title=\"Tool Kit\">Tool Kit</a> </td> \n   <td>250 </td> \n   <td>1 kg </td>\n  </tr> \n  <tr> \n   <td><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Pack\" title=\"Power Pack\">Power Pack</a> </td> \n   <td>25 </td> \n   <td>0.1 kg </td>\n  </tr> \n  <tr> \n   <td><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Energy_Cell\" title=\"Energy Cell\">Energy Cell</a> </td> \n   <td>10 </td> \n   <td>- </td>\n  </tr> \n  <tr> \n   <td><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Glow_Rod\" title=\"Glow Rod\">Glow Rod</a> </td> \n   <td>10 </td> \n   <td>1 kg </td>\n  </tr> \n  <tr> \n   <td><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Comlink\" title=\"Comlink\">Comlink</a> (Short-Range) </td> \n   <td>25 </td> \n   <td>0.1 kg </td>\n  </tr> \n  <tr> \n   <td><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Liquid_Cable_Dispenser\" title=\"Liquid Cable Dispenser\">Liquid Cable Dispenser</a> (With Small Grappling Hook) </td> \n   <td>10 </td> \n   <td>0.2 kg </td>\n  </tr>\n </tbody>\n</table><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Homebrew_Notes\">Homebrew Notes</span></h2><table style=\"width:100%; margin-top:2em; border:2px solid #999; font-size:105%; text-align:center; background:#6c3636;\"> \n <tbody>\n  <tr> \n   <td><i><b>This <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Homebrew_Content\" title=\"Homebrew Content\">Homebrew Content</a> has not been reviewed in a meaningful manner. If you wish to review this content yourself, then see <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Untested\" title=\"Category:Untested\">Untested</a> for more details.</b></i> </td>\n  </tr>\n </tbody>\n</table><p>If the cost and weight of all the individual items inside the Utility Belt were subtracted from the Utility Belt's weight and cost, it would have the following statistics: </p><p>The Utility Belt has several items over the specified 0.5 kg weight (<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Medpac\" title=\"Medpac\">Medpac</a>, <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Tool_Kit\" title=\"Tool Kit\">Tool Kit</a>, and <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Glow_Rod\" title=\"Glow Rod\">Glow Rod</a>). No official reason has been given as to why these items are allowed to \"Outweigh\" the belt. The Gamemaster may have you use any of the following fan-speculated solutions to this discrepancy or ignore it altogether: </p><ul>\n <li>Items over the specified weight hang off the Utility Belt and the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Ration_Pack\" title=\"Ration Pack\">Ration Packs</a> are in separate pouches, leaving 3 empty pouches at purchase.</li> \n <li>The Utility Belt has a maximum weight capacity of 5 kg, but can only have 10 different items.</li>\n</ul>",
